!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/a-dependent-type-as-an-explicit-choice-variant-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §4.2, [TSON-SCHEMA] §5.2, [TSON-SCHEMA] §5.4"
  description: """
    A dependent type stands in place directly at a record field's type and at no other slot, its record being what
    binds `on`. Written as one of a choice's `variants`, even inside the type of a field of a record that declares
    `kind` before it, `{ of: !meta.dependent { on: kind } }` is refused at the declaration. A choice holding one
    cannot be disjoint either, the type the sibling names being any type, so §5.4 refuses the same choice for a
    second reason.
    """
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
